by nicolas-grekas at 2026-10-11T12:25:02Z

Thank you @ayyoub-afwallah, I updated the PR. The resolver is now `RateLimitValueResolver`, like `LockValueResolver`, and it throws a `LogicException` when no `#[RateLimit]` applies. It's also removed when rate limiting is disabled.

I dropped `#[MapRateLimit]` for now. `exposed` filters on a header setting, which a controller shouldn't care about. And with `#[RateLimit('daily', key: 'a')]` and `#[RateLimit('daily', key: 'b')]`, `#[MapRateLimit('daily')]` always gets the most restrictive of the two, so `limiter` can't select one attribute. We can add an attribute later without breaking BC, once a use case needs it.

